sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor U as User
  participant B as Browser<br/>Next.js (Vercel)
  participant G as API Gateway<br/>HTTP API
  participant C as Lambda<br/>createNotification
  participant D as DynamoDB<br/>notification-requests
  participant Q as SQS<br/>notification-requests
  participant W as Lambda<br/>processNotifications
  participant P as Provider<br/>(simulated)

  U->>B: Fill in user, recipient, subject, message
  B->>B: Validate with the shared zod schema
  B->>G: POST /notifications
  G->>C: Invoke (sync)
  C->>C: Validate again (authoritative)
  C->>D: PutItem status=PENDING<br/>(cond: id does not exist)
  C->>Q: SendMessage { notificationId }
  alt SQS accepted
    C->>D: UpdateItem PENDING → QUEUED
    C-->>B: 202 Accepted + Location
  else SQS send failed
    C->>D: UpdateItem PENDING → FAILED
    C-->>B: 503 ENQUEUE_FAILED
  end

  Note over Q,W: Event source mapping polls the queue, batches of ≤ 10
  Q->>W: Invoke with SQS records
  W->>D: UpdateItem → PROCESSING, attempts + 1<br/>(cond: status allows claim, attempts < 3)
  W->>P: send(notification)
  alt Provider accepted
    W->>D: UpdateItem → SENT, providerMessageId, completedAt
    W-->>Q: Message deleted
  else Transient error, attempts left
    W->>D: UpdateItem → QUEUED, lastError
    W-->>Q: Batch item failure → redelivered after 60 s
  else Permanent error, or 3rd failure
    W->>D: UpdateItem → FAILED, lastError, completedAt
    W-->>Q: Message deleted
  end

  loop Every 2 s while any request is in flight
    B->>G: GET /notifications (?userId=)
    G->>D: Query byCreatedAt / byUser index
    G-->>B: 200 { data, nextCursor }
  end
